     1,
     "Dear all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m wondering if you know why are some of the days are not adding up to 1440 seconds? The device was worn for 7 consecutive days (codes were set to &quot;MM&quot;).</div><div><br></div><div>For instance, one participant&#39;s (who did not have non-wear time recorded in the log) part 2  day summary report is as follows:</div><div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"94\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:70pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" width=\"94\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt;width:70pt\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"115\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:86pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" width=\"115\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt;width:86pt\">N valid hours</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>23.75</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>12.75</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>0</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br></span></span></span><br>N hours</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>23.75</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>24</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>8.5</span></span></span></div><div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"94\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:70pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br></span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\">The same participants&#39;s part 5 personal summary report: </span></span></span></div><div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"94\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:70pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"187\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:140pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" width=\"187\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt;width:140pt\">dur_day_spt_min_wei</span></span><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br>1436.429</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"94\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:70pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"187\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:140pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br></span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div>In the part 5 personal summary report, some participants had the full 1440 seconds, while others had less than 1440 seconds. </div><div><br></div><div>Does this mean GGIR only capture valid hours, instead of the device wearing hours? Is there anyway I could set the codes to get the full 1440 seconds?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you for your time.</div><div><br></div><div>Kind Regards,</div><div><br></div><div>Jaslie</div><div><span border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"94\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:70pt\"><span height=\"19\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><span height=\"19\" align=\"right\" style=\"min-height:14.4pt\"><br></span></span></span></div>"
    ]
   ]
