   "subject": "Re: [GGIR] reports of valid number of hours VS device wearing hours",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Hi Jaslie,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Most likely GGIR ignores the first 15 minutes of the first day because the recording started just after midnight? If yes, then it always uses all data from the first full long epoch window onward, which is why it shows 23.75 hour (23:45 in clock time).</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">The last day is incomplete because your recording does not end at the end of the day. However, this day should be excluded in part 5 MM report because it by default only include days that have 23 or more hours of data.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">This then also explains why the person level average is not exactly 1440 minutes.</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Regards,</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">Vincent</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px\">\r\n    <div>\r\n        <div><div><br></div></div></div></div><div></div>"
    ],
    [
